WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:52.970
<b>Luffy vs. Mr. 3</b>

3
00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:55.220
Zoro... Why are you
standing like that?

4
00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:57.450
If I'm gonna be a statue,
I prefer this pose.

5
00:01:57.470 --> 00:01:59.640
This is no time
to be playing around!

6
00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:01.450
Do you think you could at least

7
00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:03.100
do something about
all this blood?

8
00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:04.650
I'm getting nauseous
just looking at it.

9
00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:06.060
[ZORO]
So quit lookin' at it, then.

10
00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:08.110
[NAMI]
It's kind of hard to ignore.

11
00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:09.880
Do you still think
it was a bright idea

12
00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:12.550
to cut your own legs off so
that we could escape from here?

13
00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:13.920
[ZORO]
That wasn't the point.

14
00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.370
I was going to cut them off
so that we could fight.

15
00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:17.630
Oh, was that the plan?

16
00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:19.830
'Cause that's an
even worse idea!

17
00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:21.270
Whatever...

18
00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:23.620
Seriously, sometimes
I think you were born

19
00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:26.300
without any common
sense at all.

20
00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:29.070
[VIVI]
We're stuck here about
to be turned into wax statues,

21
00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:30.930
and the two of
them are bickering!

22
00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:32.900
They really don't seem
to understand the danger

23
00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:35.000
of the situation at all.

24
00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:39.270
Hey, sword guy...

25
00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:41.820
Is that all the fight
you got left in ya?

26
00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:43.650
Yeah, I think I'm gonna
have to let someone else

27
00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:45.820
take over from here.

28
00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:49.930
They don't seem terribly worried

29
00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:52.190
about what's going to happen
to them, Mr. 3.

30
00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:53.950
[MR. 3]
And you don't
seem terribly worried

31
00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:56.990
about making sure it happens,
Miss Golden Week.

32
00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:59.260
[MR. 3]
Solidify already...

33
00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:00.920
If you wanna die
in a cool pose, Nami,

34
00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:01.990
you'd better hurry up.

35
00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:03.440
Mr. Bushido, could you
please take this

36
00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:05.020
a little more seriously?

37
00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:07.090
Hey, your pose could use
a little work, too.

38
00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:09.230
Shut up about
the posing already!

39
00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:10.890
They're acting so
careless like this

40
00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:12.830
for no other reason
than to mock us!

41
00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:14.380
This is very annoying!

42
00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:17.300
All right!

43
00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:18.630
[MR. 3]
Though he doesn't seem to be

44
00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:22.160
a very reliable man...
If you ask me.

45
00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:23.500
[MR. 5]
Mr. 5.

46
00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:24.570
[MR. 3]
Hm?

47
00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:26.230
We'll be happy to take care
of the Straw Hat pest.

48
00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:29.140
[MR. 3]
Hmph. Take care of him?

49
00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:31.110
Please. Don't be ridiculous.

50
00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.510
I sent you to take care
of him once already,

51
00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:35.950
and look! He's standing in
front of us alive and well,

52
00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:38.180
interfering with my
artistic process.

53
00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:40.120
I think it's clear that
you can't handle him.

54
00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:43.330
He's obviously too much
for you, wouldn't you agree?

55
00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:45.010
[growls]

56
00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:46.480
You two can deal
with the others.

57
00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:49.010
If you think you're
up to it, that is.

58
00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:50.510
I'll take care of him.

59
00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:52.450
I think a Straw Hat Luffy
statue would make

60
00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:54.620
an excellent addition
to my collection.

61
00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:59.550
I think I've had way
more than enough of you.

62
00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:03.070
And if you cretins know
what's good for ya,

63
00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:04.220
you'll give up now.

64
00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.390
[squawks]

65
00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.860
'Kay, we're safely
in position now.

66
00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:13.120
We got your back
from here, Luffy!

67
00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:14.220
[squawks]

68
00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.860
[LUFFY]
Hm? Did you say something?

69
00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:20.190
[MR. 3]
Now I've
got you! Candle... Lock!

70
00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:23.900
[yelping]

71
00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.200
[gasps]

72
00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.370
What's he doing?

73
00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:27.870
[squawks]

74
00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:28.570
[LUFFY grunts]

75
00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:29.620
[VIVI]
Luffy!

76
00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.790
[ZORO]
Damn! He got caught already?

77
00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:34.110
[NAMI]
Moron!

78
00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:35.270
What is this thing?

79
00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:37.210
Whatever it is,
it's nice and heavy.

80
00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:39.110
[MR. 3]
Almost too simple...

81
00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:43.080
All right, just once more.

82
00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.850
[LUFFY]
Hm...

83
00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:49.020
Yeah! This should be perfect!

84
00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:51.120
Candle... Lock!

85
00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:51.890
[yelps]

86
00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:53.130
[LUFFY]
Whoa!

87
00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:00.800
[LUFFY]
Hey, giant guy!

88
00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.710
Excuse me!

89
00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:05.140
Uh... What the...?

90
00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:07.480
What is this weirdo doing now?

91
00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:16.620
[gasps]

92
00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.950
[LUFFY]
Gum-Gum...

93
00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:20.790
Mallet!

94
00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:24.930
[yelps]

95
00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:26.640
[VIVI, NAMI]
– All right!
– All right!

96
00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.630
[VIVI, NAMI, ZORO scream]

97
00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:34.800
[NAMI, VIVI screaming]

98
00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:41.880
[VIVI, ZORO, NAMI whimpering]

99
00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:47.750
Hey, the thing on my legs
broke at the same time.

100
00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:49.000
Huh?

101
00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:51.510
[LUFFY]
Um, but wait...

102
00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:54.450
Why are they still there?

103
00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:57.820
[panting]

104
00:05:57.820 --> 00:05:59.190
We're okay now.

105
00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:01.190
[sighs]

106
00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:02.920
We didn't die.

107
00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:03.720
We're still alive

108
00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:06.170
but that really
didn't help at all.

109
00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:07.340
That was a close one!

110
00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:09.410
But why didn't
you guys run away?

111
00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:10.810
[VIVI, NAMI]
– Because we're stuck here!
– Because we're stuck here!

112
00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:12.040
Isn't that obvious?!

113
00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:13.080
Oh, really?

114
00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:14.710
So that's what's going on?

115
00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:16.040
The only thing
you guys kept saying

116
00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:17.880
was that I needed to
break the pillar...

117
00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:18.880
Mr. Bushido!

118
00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:20.640
Do you really think it's
a good idea to put our lives

119
00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:22.360
in that guy's hands?

120
00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:25.160
Well, we don't exactly have
much of a choice, do we?

121
00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:26.360
I don't know about you,

122
00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.540
but I'm having a little bit
of trouble moving right now...

123
00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:33.140
I... can't move...

124
00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:37.640
What's happening?
My body... I don't know...

125
00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:43.170
It... It won't move...
I can't move at all...

126
00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:43.140
[Mr. 3 cackles]

127
00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:44.370
[MR. 3]
You fools!

128
00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:49.390
[MR. 3]
You fools!

129
00:06:49.390 --> 00:06:51.990
All you did was move
the candles closer!

130
00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:55.290
And by doing so, you only sped
up the solidifying process.

131
00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:57.630
You'll become wax figures
even sooner, now!

132
00:06:57.630 --> 00:06:59.200
Well done!

133
00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:01.230
Ugh! That guy!

134
00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:03.700
I wanna punch him,
right in his smug little face!

135
00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:04.870
[squawks]

136
00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:07.990
[LUFFY]
Wait! You guys are
gonna turn into wax figures?

137
00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:10.240
[NAMI]
That's what we've
been trying to tell you!

138
00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:13.160
[VIVI]
Please just hurry up
and destroy this thing, Luffy!

139
00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.460
[LUFFY]
Right, yeah, I'm on it!

140
00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:16.580
[MR. 3]
I don't think so, Straw Hat!

141
00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:18.420
Now, get out of my way!

142
00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:20.650
Wax-Wax... Harpoon!

143
00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:21.850
Exploding Star!

144
00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:23.350
[gasps]

145
00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:30.290
[MR. 5 gulps]

146
00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:32.100
[LUFFY yelps]

147
00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:47.050
That's not very flavorful.

148
00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:49.290
Your gunpowder must
not be too good.

149
00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:52.360
There's no way! He ate it!

150
00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:54.960
[squawks]

151
00:07:56.130 --> 00:07:59.080
[ZORO]
This isn't really
looking good for us, ladies...

152
00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.080
This damn thing is speeding up.

153
00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.050
Good thing I've
got my pose ready.

154
00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:03.820
Moron!

155
00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:07.290
Come on, Luffy!
You have to hurry!

156
00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:11.160
Right! So the pumpkin
thing has to go.

157
00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:13.230
I'm on it now! Gum-Gum...

158
00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:16.500
[MR. 3]
It's no use! Candle... Wall!

159
00:08:18.110 --> 00:08:20.640
Bazooka!

160
00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:25.070
Hey! Outta my way!

161
00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:27.650
I was just thinking
the same thing.

162
00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:30.410
I would greatly appreciate it
if you would quit interfering

163
00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:33.980
with my creative
activities. Candle Lock!

164
00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:38.290
I got a mallet...

165
00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:39.470
[MR. 3]
Huh?

166
00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:41.580
[LUFFY]
Gum-Gum...

167
00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.980
No you don't! Candle Wall!

168
00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:45.810
[LUFFY]
Mallet!

169
00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:56.140
[MR. 3 whimpers]

170
00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:59.040
[MR. 3 screams]

171
00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:05.250
M-Mr. 3?!

172
00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:06.820
No way!

173
00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:10.370
[NAMI]
Luffy! Hurry up
and break this thing

174
00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:12.250
before we die up here!

175
00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:13.250
Um, no...

176
00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:15.780
Quit joking around and hurry.

177
00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:16.580
[LUFFY]
Nuh-uh.

178
00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:18.550
[ZORO gasps]
Quit being an idiot!

179
00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:20.620
Now's not really a good time!

180
00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:22.960
[VIVI]
Luffy! Please just do it!

181
00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:24.290
Not now... I...

182
00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:27.160
...just don't feel
like saving you.

183
00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:30.830
[pants]

184
00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:33.490
Luffy, what's wrong?

185
00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:36.700
My Colors Trap.

186
00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:40.270
[ZORO]
Hey, Luffy!

187
00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:42.040
There's no time
to space out now!

188
00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:44.010
Do somethin' about this already!

189
00:09:44.010 --> 00:09:45.510
[LUFFY]
Yeah... I know.

190
00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:47.410
[VIVI]
Then quit just
standing there, will you?

191
00:09:47.410 --> 00:09:49.950
[NAMI]
Come on, Luffy!

192
00:09:49.950 --> 00:09:51.450
I know what I should do.

193
00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:54.290
But... I don't feel like it...

194
00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:56.120
Damn it! Why do you
keep saying that?

195
00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.530
We're about to be
turned into wax statues!

196
00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:00.830
Do you understand me?
We're going to die!

197
00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:01.960
[LUFFY]
Yeah...

198
00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:05.080
But for some reason, I can't
get motivated to help...

199
00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.740
[ALL]
– What do you mean, "can't get motivated"?!
– What do you mean, "can't get motivated"?!

200
00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:13.750
What's going on here?
What is wrong with him?

201
00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:15.150
Our friends are gonna
die if he doesn't

202
00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:17.250
do something to help them soon.

203
00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:20.890
I'll snap him out of it.

204
00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:22.060
Let's go, Karoo.

205
00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:23.390
[squawks]

206
00:10:24.860 --> 00:10:25.860
Huh?

207
00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:28.230
[USOPP]
Where did you two come from?!

208
00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:29.900
Just give up.

209
00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:31.860
Your friend has already
fallen into a nasty trap.

210
00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:32.930
That's right.

211
00:10:32.930 --> 00:10:35.070
Haven't you noticed
what he's standing on?

212
00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:36.600
Standing?

213
00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:39.260
[USOPP]
Let me take a look.

214
00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:40.810
[USOPP]
What's that? There's a strange

215
00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:42.760
black pattern on the ground.

216
00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:43.620
I don't get it.

217
00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:45.830
What's so important
about that thing?

218
00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:46.730
Yeah, you're right.

219
00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:48.830
You really don't get it
at all, do you?

220
00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:51.630
[laughs]

221
00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:53.570
What's funny?

222
00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:56.770
Paint... That's what's funny.

223
00:10:56.770 --> 00:10:58.400
It's just paint...

224
00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:01.610
You and your friends don't
stand a chance of escapin' now.

225
00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:04.940
[USOPP screams]

226
00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:07.400
[screaming]

227
00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:13.040
[laughs]

228
00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:13.740
[USOPP]

229
00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:14.610
[KAROO screaming]

230
00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:16.680
Karoo! Let's make a run for it!

231
00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:18.510
[squawks]

232
00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:20.620
Oh, great, now
they're running away.

233
00:11:20.830 --> 00:11:21.620
Lets get 'em.

234
00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:28.000
Full speed ahead, Karoo!

235
00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:30.030
[squawks]

236
00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:34.060
Hey, wait! I'm not on yet!

237
00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:35.860
Slow down, Karoo! Let me on!

238
00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:37.200
Hey, bird, do you hear me?

239
00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:37.900
Let me on!

240
00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:39.530
[squawks]

241
00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:42.130
Just let me on, now!

242
00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:47.340
[USOPP panting]

243
00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:48.570
[USOPP]
Why are you afraid of me?

244
00:11:48.570 --> 00:11:50.350
I thought you were
a duck, not a chicken!

245
00:11:50.350 --> 00:11:52.290
Slow down, will you?!
Please, Karoo!

246
00:11:57.950 --> 00:11:59.780
Miss Golden Week's responsible!

247
00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:01.950
I know that this is your doing!

248
00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:04.400
It's my Colors Trap.

249
00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:06.570
Betrayal Black.

250
00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:07.380
If you touch the paint,

251
00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:09.100
you'll want to
betray your friends,

252
00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:11.010
no matter what they might say.

253
00:12:11.010 --> 00:12:13.740
Even if they beg
and plead for help.

254
00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:15.110
What's she talking about?

255
00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:17.250
I don't understand
what's going on here.

256
00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:18.280
She's a painter.

257
00:12:18.280 --> 00:12:20.450
She uses her paint to
create different emotions.

258
00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:22.120
Each color is a feeling.

259
00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:23.620
[NAMI]
Huh?

260
00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:25.240
Her sense of
color's so complete,

261
00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:26.620
she can manipulate your mind.

262
00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:28.330
Just a splash of
one of her colors,

263
00:12:28.360 --> 00:12:30.700
and you'll be
under her control.

264
00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:33.670
Under her control?!
Well, that's not good.

265
00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:36.430
That simpleminded oaf is
already too easy to control.

266
00:12:36.430 --> 00:12:39.170
The last thing we need is
someone messing with his mind.

267
00:12:39.170 --> 00:12:41.140
Does that mean that all
he needs to do is get away

268
00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:43.170
from the paint
and he'll be okay?

269
00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:45.550
Luffy! Move away
from there, quickly!

270
00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:47.710
[VIVI]
No, don't! Luffy, listen!

271
00:12:47.710 --> 00:12:49.680
Whatever you do,
please don't step outside

272
00:12:49.710 --> 00:12:52.450
the black circle,
all right? I'm begging!

273
00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:56.090
[NAMI]
What are you saying?!

274
00:12:56.090 --> 00:12:58.430
[VIVI]
We don't want
you to save us, Luffy.

275
00:12:58.430 --> 00:13:00.380
Please, stay away from us!

276
00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:04.230
No way.

277
00:13:04.230 --> 00:13:05.470
[ZORO]
I get it now.

278
00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:07.530
We just needed to say
the exact opposite

279
00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:10.070
of what we wanted him to do.

280
00:13:10.070 --> 00:13:11.310
Oh, hey!

281
00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:15.980
What... What just happened?
I was acting really strange.

282
00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:18.010
[VIVI]
Luffy! Help us now!

283
00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:25.360
[LUFFY]
Okay! I'm on my way right now!

284
00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:28.830
Never mind. I just
wanna laugh right now!

285
00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:31.840
Luffy!

286
00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:33.010
Moron!

287
00:13:33.010 --> 00:13:34.810
What now?!

288
00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:41.020
Colors Trap again.

289
00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:42.480
Laughter Yellow.

290
00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:42.450
[laughing]

291
00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:44.580
You should not have
stepped out of the circle.

292
00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:47.730
[laughing]

293
00:13:47.730 --> 00:13:49.860
Now it's on his clothing!

294
00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:52.930
Luffy! Quick!
Take off your shirt.

295
00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:54.330
[LUFFY]
I'd love to, really.

296
00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:56.810
But right now,
I'm too busy laughing.

297
00:13:58.460 --> 00:14:01.530
[ZORO grunts]
It's getting bad.

298
00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:03.900
If the wax keeps
falling at this rate,

299
00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:06.260
we'll be lucky to stay
alive for five mintues.

300
00:14:06.260 --> 00:14:08.700
[USOPP, KAROO screaming]

301
00:14:10.630 --> 00:14:13.500
[USOPP, KAROO screaming]

302
00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:16.630
[ZORO]
Did you guys come
here just to play tag?!

303
00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:18.670
[USOPP, KAROO scream]

304
00:14:20.240 --> 00:14:22.380
[NAMI]
Look! When Usopp ran into Luffy,

305
00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:24.710
the paint smudged!

306
00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:26.710
[LUFFY panting]

307
00:14:26.710 --> 00:14:31.250
[LUFFY]
Jeez! What's going on?!
I felt all weird again!

308
00:14:33.230 --> 00:14:34.550
Hey, painter girl!

309
00:14:34.550 --> 00:14:36.550
Would you stop messin'
with me already?!

310
00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:38.390
[MISS GOLDEN WEEK]
But you
were having such a good time.

311
00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:39.240
Wasn't it funny?

312
00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:41.670
Well, yeah...
it was kinda funny.

313
00:14:41.670 --> 00:14:43.560
But stop!

314
00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:46.040
I've gotta see about
breaking that pumpkin now.

315
00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:47.670
Gum-Gum...

316
00:14:47.670 --> 00:14:49.500
[MISS GOLDEN WEEK]
Another Colors Trap!

317
00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:51.370
Time for Bullfight Red!

318
00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:54.840
[LUFFY]
Bazooka!

319
00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:56.540
[ZORO]
What were you aiming at?

320
00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:57.920
I just can't let you break it.

321
00:14:57.920 --> 00:15:00.050
Mr. 3 wouldn't be
happy about that at all.

322
00:15:00.050 --> 00:15:01.650
What'd you do?!

323
00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:02.880
During a bull fight,
a bull can't

324
00:15:02.910 --> 00:15:04.950
control his urge to
attack the red cape.

325
00:15:04.950 --> 00:15:06.740
Likewise, you can't
do anything now

326
00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:08.390
but attack that red circle.

327
00:15:08.390 --> 00:15:09.760
That's what I did.

328
00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:10.570
[screams]

329
00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:12.260
'Kay, that does it!

330
00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:14.210
I'm mad now!

331
00:15:14.210 --> 00:15:15.370
Gum-Gum...

332
00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:18.180
Bazooka!

333
00:15:19.400 --> 00:15:20.360
Having fun?

334
00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:23.150
Aw... Oh, great...

335
00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:25.680
At this rate, he's never
gonna be able to beat her.

336
00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:28.320
Now all of his
strength is useless.

337
00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:29.250
[MISS GOLDEN WEEK]
Now to finish up!

338
00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:31.140
We'll mix the Laughter
Yellow on your back

339
00:15:31.170 --> 00:15:33.350
with some Sadness Blue!

340
00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:36.850
The last Colors Trap:
Tranquil Green.

341
00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:40.670
[sighs]

342
00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:45.340
Ah... That's some good tea!

343
00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:47.880
[NAMI, ZORO, VIVI]
– Luffy!
– Luffy!

344
00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:50.220
So... What happens now?

345
00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:51.720
See, I told you,
you should have posed,

346
00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:53.860
but you wouldn't listen to me.
And now it's too late.

347
00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:55.360
You're gonna die like that.

348
00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:57.160
Are you really still
talking about that?

349
00:16:09.470 --> 00:16:12.100
Damn. How can they just
keep runnin' like that?

350
00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:19.510
Nose Fancy Double Cannon!

351
00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:23.370
[KAROO squawks]

352
00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:27.170
[USOPP laughs]
You missed us,
jerk! Way to go, Karoo!

353
00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:28.020
[KAROO squawks]

354
00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:31.300
My turn now!

355
00:16:31.450 --> 00:16:33.460
Special Attack: Lead Star!

356
00:16:36.330 --> 00:16:38.400
[USOPP]
We need to get back
to Luffy and the others now.

357
00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:39.500
[KAROO squawks]

358
00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:43.900
Chasin' them around
isn't gettin us anywhere.

359
00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:45.300
I noticed.

360
00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:52.950
I hate to use this on
useless pests like them,

361
00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:55.950
but it looks like we may
not have a choice now.

362
00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:57.920
This little beauty
should be quite handy.

363
00:16:57.920 --> 00:17:00.990
A .44-caliber, six-shot,
flintlock revolver.

364
00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:04.100
It's a new model out
of the South Blue.

365
00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:06.100
Continuous fire.

366
00:17:06.100 --> 00:17:08.800
And when I shoot it,
the bullets are invisible.

367
00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:11.860
[USOPP]
When Luffy was acting
so strange back there,

368
00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:15.050
those two agents mentioned
something about paint.

369
00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:18.020
The paint must have something
to do with Luffy's behavior!

370
00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:19.870
There was also some
yellow paint on his back

371
00:17:19.870 --> 00:17:21.790
when we crashed
into him earlier.

372
00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:23.260
That's gotta be the key!

373
00:17:23.260 --> 00:17:25.040
We just have to do
something about the paint

374
00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:26.560
before it's too late!

375
00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:27.260
[USOPP]
Hurry!

376
00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:28.770
[KAROO squawks]

377
00:17:43.550 --> 00:17:48.310
[LUFFY sighs]
This really is some nice tea.

378
00:17:49.690 --> 00:17:50.630
Luffy!

379
00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:55.030
Hey! Wake up!

380
00:17:55.030 --> 00:18:01.060
It's nice tea...
So nice... Very nice.

381
00:18:01.060 --> 00:18:02.640
Why are you sitting there...

382
00:18:03.340 --> 00:18:05.530
...and drinking tea?!

383
00:18:08.920 --> 00:18:11.920
Run all you want. It's all over
for you and your friends.

384
00:18:11.920 --> 00:18:14.660
Here comes my best trick so far!

385
00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:16.990
Special Attack: Exploding Star!

386
00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:22.590
[BOTH SCREAM]

387
00:18:22.590 --> 00:18:23.960
[MISS VALENTINE]
Ahaha

388
00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:28.530
What an idiot!

389
00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:31.400
He missed the target
and hit his friend instead.

390
00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:35.370
Good. That was the
last of his bullets.

391
00:18:38.070 --> 00:18:41.610
[MR. 5 chuckles]
Breeze Breath Bomb!

392
00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:44.410
[BOTH scream]

393
00:18:45.490 --> 00:18:48.390
Did I forget to mention that
my breath is also explosive?

394
00:18:50.410 --> 00:18:53.150
[USOPP]
Damn. I can't believe this guy!

395
00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:55.480
He didn't have any
bullets to begin with?!

396
00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:58.350
Hey, Karoo... Are you all right?

397
00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:00.210
[KAROO groans]

398
00:19:00.210 --> 00:19:02.680
[coughs]
Luffy...!
You snap out of it yet?

399
00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:05.920
[LUFFY]
Yeah. I'm good now, thanks.

400
00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:09.470
[gasps]
So he didn't miss!
His plan this whole time

401
00:19:09.470 --> 00:19:12.140
was to burn the Colors Trap
on the Straw Hat's shirt.

402
00:19:12.140 --> 00:19:13.600
[pants]

403
00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:16.230
I'm tired of your stupid paints.
You're through...

404
00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:21.900
I'm not gonna let you hurt
any more of my friends...

405
00:19:22.310 --> 00:19:23.770
[growls]
Now, I'm really mad!

406
00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:29.540
This is getting weird.
It's been a long time,

407
00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:33.650
and no one's come back.
I wonder what's going on.

408
00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:34.880
This island's crazy.

409
00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:38.290
Anything could have happened
to Nami, Vivi, and the others,

410
00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:39.790
which means that
cooking this lizard

411
00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:42.720
may have to wait for a while.

412
00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:48.330
Hey, Nami! Vivi!
Can you hear me?

413
00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:50.330
Hey! Beautiful ladies!

414
00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:52.630
If you can hear me,
please just say something!

415
00:19:58.440 --> 00:20:00.650
That's strange. What's this?

416
00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:04.120
[MR. 5 laughs]
Oh, you're mad, are ya?

417
00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:07.920
Look at your friends. Being
mad won't do them any good.

418
00:20:07.920 --> 00:20:10.020
Oh, yes, it will!
They're still alive!

419
00:20:10.320 --> 00:20:14.130
[MR. 5 laughs]
Are they, now? Look again...

420
00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:16.190
All they need is some of
Miss Golden Week's paint,

421
00:20:16.190 --> 00:20:18.500
and they'll be
perfect wax statues.

422
00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:20.930
Face it: You're too
late to save them...

423
00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:23.130
They're gone, and you know it!

424
00:20:23.130 --> 00:20:24.100
[GROWLS]

425
00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:26.270
[MR. 3]
Mr. 5 is right about that.

426
00:20:26.270 --> 00:20:28.800
Your friends are finished
because you were too late

427
00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:32.110
to help them, and now,
it's your turn to die.

428
00:20:41.220 --> 00:20:43.220
[MR. 3]
It's time for...

429
00:20:49.990 --> 00:20:52.160
[MR. 3]
...Candle...

430
00:20:53.660 --> 00:20:55.560
...Champion!

431
00:20:57.100 --> 00:20:58.360
[MR. 3 laughs]

432
00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:01.460
[screams]

433
00:21:01.460 --> 00:21:03.130
What the heck is that?

434
00:21:03.130 --> 00:21:05.500
That thing...? That is
what he used one time

435
00:21:05.500 --> 00:21:08.800
to take down someone with a
forty-two million berry bounty.

436
00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:11.130
That's Mr. 3's most
dangerous work of art.

437
00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:13.440
Time to use your talents,
Miss Golden Week.

438
00:21:13.440 --> 00:21:16.210
I need an extra special
paint job for my armor,

439
00:21:16.240 --> 00:21:18.050
and don't forget to be artistic.

440
00:21:18.050 --> 00:21:19.890
After that, can I take a break?

441
00:21:19.890 --> 00:21:21.980
[MR. 3]
Why, yes,
you can go get some tea.

442
00:21:21.980 --> 00:21:24.150
I'd prefer it if you stayed
out of this, actually.

443
00:21:24.150 --> 00:21:27.320
When I'm in this armor,
I'm utterly impervious to harm.

444
00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:28.630
This suit is as hard as iron.

445
00:21:28.630 --> 00:21:30.870
It may be made of wax,
but it fits like a glove,

446
00:21:30.870 --> 00:21:33.170
and it's impossible
for anyone to pierce.

447
00:21:33.170 --> 00:21:35.310
And you don't stand
a chance against it.

448
00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:39.310
[MR. 3]
This artwork is flawless.

449
00:21:42.580 --> 00:21:45.420
Wow...! That's so cool!

450
00:21:45.420 --> 00:21:48.850
Why are you
admiring him?! Fight!

451
00:21:49.190 --> 00:21:51.590
Just a little more
laughter yellow...

452
00:21:52.690 --> 00:21:55.530
Right! Gum-Gum...

453
00:21:57.170 --> 00:21:58.270
[MISS GOLDEN WEEK]
Paint job complete!

454
00:21:58.270 --> 00:21:58.970
And now...

455
00:21:58.970 --> 00:22:01.440
[LUFFY]
...Pistol!

456
00:22:03.410 --> 00:22:07.840
...Champion Fight:
Harvest Field Maneuver.

457
00:22:09.350 --> 00:22:11.380
[LUFFY]
Gum-Gum...

458
00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:14.880
[LUFFY]
...Stamp!

459
00:22:19.040 --> 00:22:20.250
Hehe! Nice try!

460
00:22:20.250 --> 00:22:21.380
Not good!

461
00:22:21.380 --> 00:22:24.220
Luffy's attacks don't work
against that guy's armor!

462
00:22:28.390 --> 00:22:32.090
[coughs]
The wax is choking me! Huh?

463
00:22:34.490 --> 00:22:35.920
Wax... Huh...

464
00:22:38.510 --> 00:22:43.230
[USOPP]
Of course...! Why didn't
I realize it before now?

465
00:22:43.230 --> 00:22:44.630
It's all wax,

466
00:22:44.920 --> 00:22:47.660
which means that
it must be able to melt!

467
00:22:48.230 --> 00:22:50.240
[USOPP]
Luffy, we need to use fire!

468
00:22:50.770 --> 00:22:53.100
No matter how hard it is,
wax is still wax!

469
00:22:53.700 --> 00:22:55.610
The others only hardened
a few moments ago...!

470
00:22:55.610 --> 00:22:58.370
We should still be
able to save them!

471
00:22:58.370 --> 00:22:59.240
Quack!

472
00:22:59.240 --> 00:23:00.950
No way! Seriously?!

473
00:23:00.950 --> 00:23:01.880
[MISS GOLDEN WEEK]
Yeah, that's correct.

474
00:23:01.880 --> 00:23:05.650
Aaaaah! You idiot!
Don't tell them that!

475
00:23:05.650 --> 00:23:08.120
But it doesn't really matter
if you realize that now,

476
00:23:08.120 --> 00:23:09.790
you have no
hope of saving them.

477
00:23:09.790 --> 00:23:11.560
They have thirty
seconds left, at most.

478
00:23:11.560 --> 00:23:14.190
After that, their hearts
will slow to a stop.

479
00:23:14.190 --> 00:23:16.160
As we speak, they're
writhing in silent pain,

480
00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:17.150
barely conscious...

481
00:23:17.150 --> 00:23:19.260
They're hanging onto
their lives by a thread,

482
00:23:19.290 --> 00:23:20.990
terrified of
their impending doom

483
00:23:20.990 --> 00:23:22.990
and unable to move or
even scream for help...!

484
00:23:22.990 --> 00:23:28.030
And they know that you were too
late to save them! Hahahaha!

485
00:23:28.030 --> 00:23:31.630
I'll save 'em right now.
I don't need thirty seconds.

486
00:23:32.700 --> 00:23:34.740
Breeze Breath Bomb!

487
00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:38.040
[USOPP screams]

488
00:23:38.040 --> 00:23:41.210
Usopp! No!

489
00:23:41.210 --> 00:23:44.050
Quaaaack!

490
00:23:44.050 --> 00:23:45.850
When we say you
don't stand a chance,

491
00:23:45.880 --> 00:23:46.920
it's best to believe us.

492
00:23:49.630 --> 00:23:50.630
[GRUNTS]

493
00:23:50.630 --> 00:23:52.800
[LUFFY]
Damn it!
We're running out of time!

494
00:23:54.620 --> 00:23:55.410
[MR. 3]
Just give up.

495
00:24:02.970 --> 00:24:05.910
Listen, I need you to grab
a hold of this rope, Karoo.

496
00:24:05.910 --> 00:24:08.480
[MISS VALENTINE]
Well, this looks like a party.

497
00:24:08.480 --> 00:24:10.450
Now what are
you two planning...?

498
00:24:10.450 --> 00:24:12.580
Do you think I could
join in on the fun?

499
00:24:15.850 --> 00:24:18.250
Karoo, run now.

500
00:24:18.250 --> 00:24:19.820
Get going!

501
00:24:19.820 --> 00:24:21.260
[USOPP]
Just run around
all the candle sticks!

502
00:24:21.260 --> 00:24:23.490
And move as quick as you can!

503
00:24:25.990 --> 00:24:28.680
Come on.
I don't know why you bother.

504
00:24:28.680 --> 00:24:29.550
[MISS VALENTINE]
'Scuse me.

505
00:24:29.550 --> 00:24:30.610
Ah, jeez.

506
00:24:30.610 --> 00:24:34.740
[MISS VALENTINE]
Can you
handle my Crescendo Stone?

507
00:24:34.740 --> 00:24:37.990
I wonder just how many kilograms
you'll be able to endure.

508
00:24:37.990 --> 00:24:40.160
[KAROO]
Quaaaaack! Quack!

509
00:24:40.160 --> 00:24:41.430
[MISS VALENTINE]
Ten kilograms.

510
00:24:41.430 --> 00:24:43.100
[USOPP groans]

511
00:24:43.100 --> 00:24:44.600
[MISS VALENTINE]
One hundred kilograms.

512
00:24:44.600 --> 00:24:47.100
[USOPP groans]

513
00:24:48.150 --> 00:24:50.280
[MISS VALENTINE]
Two hundred kilograms.

514
00:24:50.280 --> 00:24:51.230
[USOPP grunts]

515
00:24:51.260 --> 00:24:53.370
[MISS VALENTINE]
Three hundred kilograms.

516
00:24:53.370 --> 00:24:55.640
[groans]

517
00:24:56.810 --> 00:25:00.310
[MR. 5]
Damn it!
Hold still, you quacker!

518
00:25:00.310 --> 00:25:04.280
Hahaha! Give it up! It's no use!

519
00:25:04.280 --> 00:25:06.830
Your friends are a permanent
part of my collection now!

520
00:25:06.830 --> 00:25:09.570
Accept it. Hahahahaha!

521
00:25:09.570 --> 00:25:11.470
They're not!

522
00:25:11.470 --> 00:25:14.750
There's no way I'm gonna let
you have my friends, candle boy!

523
00:25:14.750 --> 00:25:15.780
I don't have any fire,

524
00:25:15.810 --> 00:25:16.980
so I'm gonna have
to borrow yours.

525
00:25:16.980 --> 00:25:18.440
I hope that's okay!

526
00:25:18.440 --> 00:25:20.980
That hurts! Quit pulling!
Stop it!

527
00:25:20.980 --> 00:25:22.140
Hold on!

528
00:25:22.140 --> 00:25:24.410
That tiny little flame isn't
gonna work quickly enough!

529
00:25:24.450 --> 00:25:26.080
[USOPP]
The rope that Karoo has...

530
00:25:26.080 --> 00:25:27.750
Light that on fire!

531
00:25:27.750 --> 00:25:29.900
A rope? How's that
supposed to help us?

532
00:25:29.900 --> 00:25:31.930
Just trust me on this!

533
00:25:31.960 --> 00:25:32.950
[LUFFY]
Huh?

534
00:25:32.980 --> 00:25:35.460
I covered the
whole thing in oil.

535
00:25:35.490 --> 00:25:38.090
[LUFFY]
Okay, everyone,
it's time to wake up!

536
00:25:38.090 --> 00:25:39.810
It'll be hot,
but it's the only way,

537
00:25:39.840 --> 00:25:41.460
and they should be all right.

538
00:25:41.460 --> 00:25:43.710
Stop it! Let go! Aaaaaa!

539
00:25:44.460 --> 00:25:48.100
[LUFFY roars]

540
00:25:57.610 --> 00:26:01.140
Aaaaah! Ahhh

541
00:26:01.140 --> 00:26:02.810
Uh, whoops...!

542
00:26:02.810 --> 00:26:05.450
Hope the others don't
get all burned up!

543
00:26:06.050 --> 00:26:09.620
[MR. 3]
Oh, curse you, you
stupid Straw Hat pirate!

544
00:26:09.620 --> 00:26:12.020
You destroyed
my precious candle set...!

545
00:26:12.020 --> 00:26:15.660
How dare you show such disregard
for artistic integrity!

546
00:26:17.130 --> 00:26:18.890
[MR. 3]
You'll pay for this!

547
00:26:19.960 --> 00:26:21.960
No! You're not getting
away with this...

548
00:26:21.960 --> 00:26:24.820
Quaaaaack! Quaaaaack!

549
00:26:24.820 --> 00:26:25.720
[MR. 5]
Damn it...

550
00:26:26.420 --> 00:26:29.090
How dare you mock
Baroque Works agents?!

551
00:26:30.580 --> 00:26:33.790
I'm sick and tired of you
and your friends! Got that?

552
00:26:34.910 --> 00:26:36.780
Okay, playtime
is really over now!

553
00:26:37.680 --> 00:26:39.200
I'm going to break
that scrawny little neck

554
00:26:39.230 --> 00:26:41.820
of yours into a million pieces!

555
00:26:41.820 --> 00:26:42.900
Ten Thousand...

556
00:26:42.930 --> 00:26:44.810
Kilogram Guillotine!

557
00:26:55.090 --> 00:26:55.990
[NAMI]
That was really hot!

558
00:26:55.990 --> 00:26:58.590
Couldn't you have
thought up another plan?

559
00:27:02.430 --> 00:27:04.330
You're being a little
picky here, don't you think?

560
00:27:04.330 --> 00:27:06.700
Aren't you at least
a little bit grateful...?

561
00:27:06.700 --> 00:27:08.940
You have a point there. Thanks.

562
00:27:08.940 --> 00:27:11.810
It's amazing! I can't
believe we're actually alive!

563
00:27:11.810 --> 00:27:15.660
Got out of the wax, did ya?
Well, I've had enough...

564
00:27:15.660 --> 00:27:20.400
We simply cannot afford for you
to screw up our mission anymore.

565
00:27:20.740 --> 00:27:22.250
[USOPP]
Hey, Mr. 5!

566
00:27:22.750 --> 00:27:26.650
Special Attack...
Exploding Star!

567
00:27:26.650 --> 00:27:27.760
You fool!
Haven't you figured out

568
00:27:27.760 --> 00:27:30.590
that your pathetic explosives
don't affect me at all?

569
00:27:30.590 --> 00:27:32.660
They're nothing to
an exploding man!

570
00:27:32.660 --> 00:27:34.700
You took the bait!

571
00:27:36.790 --> 00:27:38.960
I'm sorry.
I just told a little lie.

572
00:27:38.960 --> 00:27:40.690
That wasn't an Exploding Star...

573
00:27:40.690 --> 00:27:43.370
That was a Special Tabasco Star.

574
00:27:43.680 --> 00:27:46.810
[MR. 5]
Spicy

575
00:27:46.850 --> 00:27:48.020
Haha

576
00:27:49.620 --> 00:27:53.090
I had to learn how effective
that thing was the hard way!

577
00:27:53.090 --> 00:27:54.420
[MR. 5 grunts]

578
00:27:54.420 --> 00:27:56.390
Damn, you stupid pirate!

579
00:27:56.390 --> 00:27:57.720
[coughs]

580
00:27:57.720 --> 00:27:58.590
[USOPP gasps]

581
00:27:58.590 --> 00:28:00.890
[MR. 5]
Time for a full body explosion!

582
00:28:00.890 --> 00:28:03.100
There'll be nothing
left of you.

583
00:28:03.100 --> 00:28:04.730
[USOPP]
Ow...
Ow, let go of me!

584
00:28:04.730 --> 00:28:07.000
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!
Please let go!

585
00:28:07.000 --> 00:28:08.000
Let him go!

586
00:28:08.000 --> 00:28:10.000
I'm too young to die...
I'm too young to die...

587
00:28:10.000 --> 00:28:11.940
Ahhh! Let go!

588
00:28:18.010 --> 00:28:20.700
[ZORO]
Flaming Oni Giri...

589
00:28:20.830 --> 00:28:22.600
[MR. 5]
Huh

590
00:28:22.600 --> 00:28:23.630
Oh

591
00:28:23.630 --> 00:28:24.630
[ZORO GRUNTS]

592
00:28:24.630 --> 00:28:27.770
[MR. 5 SCREAMS]

593
00:28:38.930 --> 00:28:41.600
[ZORO]
You know these
flaming swords aren't too bad.

594
00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:49.120
[NAMI]
Zoro!

595
00:28:52.350 --> 00:28:54.450
[BROGY grunts]

596
00:29:00.070 --> 00:29:01.870
Hey, there. Glad to see
you made it out alive.

597
00:29:01.870 --> 00:29:03.470
Heh. Yeah.

598
00:29:13.400 --> 00:29:14.570
Master?

599
00:29:14.820 --> 00:29:19.730
So now it seems...
two foes are left.

600
00:29:21.860 --> 00:29:22.750
[LUFFY]
Bird guy! Lets go

601
00:29:22.750 --> 00:29:24.320
[KAROO]
Quack! Quack!

602
00:29:24.490 --> 00:29:26.160
They won't get off so easy!

603
00:29:27.500 --> 00:29:29.960
Real men don't interfere
with someone else's fight!

604
00:29:32.520 --> 00:29:33.920
[MR. 3 LAUGHS]

605
00:29:36.730 --> 00:29:40.700
[MR. 3]
So good of you to
come, I've been expecting you...

606
00:29:40.700 --> 00:29:43.310
Welcome to my Wax-Wax Manor.

607
00:29:43.310 --> 00:29:44.910
[LUFFY]
What's going on?

608
00:29:44.910 --> 00:29:47.710
[MR. 3]
Why, just a little
game of hide and seek...

609
00:29:47.710 --> 00:29:49.580
Can you figure out
which one is me?

610
00:29:49.580 --> 00:29:51.990
[laughs]

611
00:29:51.990 --> 00:29:54.630
I'd say it appears you picked
the wrong group of people

612
00:29:54.660 --> 00:29:55.960
to go up against.

613
00:29:55.960 --> 00:29:58.340
You're no match for
my intellectual prowess

614
00:29:58.380 --> 00:29:59.550
and artistic abilities.

615
00:29:59.550 --> 00:30:02.890
You're just another buffoon
who acts on blind instinct

616
00:30:02.890 --> 00:30:05.910
and uses brute force to
solve all his problems.

617
00:30:05.910 --> 00:30:09.140
You can't hope to catch an
intellectual giant like me!

618
00:30:09.140 --> 00:30:11.980
[laughs]

619
00:30:11.980 --> 00:30:14.750
I am a Baroque Works agent.

620
00:30:14.750 --> 00:30:18.820
Every assignment that is given
to me I see through to its end.

621
00:30:18.820 --> 00:30:21.820
So if you think you're ready,
then just step forward.

622
00:30:21.820 --> 00:30:28.730
[laughs]

623
00:30:28.730 --> 00:30:31.270
That's right;
just take a little step.

624
00:30:31.270 --> 00:30:34.080
And as soon as
your back is turned,

625
00:30:34.120 --> 00:30:35.970
I'm going to stab you...

626
00:30:35.970 --> 00:30:38.970
[laughs]

627
00:30:38.970 --> 00:30:41.390
...right through that
pathetically noble

628
00:30:41.430 --> 00:30:43.010
little heart of yours.

629
00:30:43.010 --> 00:30:45.250
[laughs]

630
00:30:50.040 --> 00:30:54.540
[LUFFY]
Gum... Stamp

631
00:30:58.110 --> 00:30:59.310
[MR. 3]
Ahh

632
00:30:59.310 --> 00:31:00.340
[GRUNTS]

633
00:31:00.340 --> 00:31:01.470
[MR. 3]
How could you have known...

634
00:31:04.740 --> 00:31:06.650
that... this...
is where I was...?

635
00:31:06.650 --> 00:31:09.150
[groans]

636
00:31:12.640 --> 00:31:14.140
Instinct.

637
00:31:14.460 --> 00:31:21.260
[SHRIEKS]

638
00:31:21.260 --> 00:31:28.090
[CLINKING GLASS]

639
00:31:34.920 --> 00:31:41.420
[SNIFFS]

640
00:31:41.420 --> 00:31:45.290
[SANJI]
Earl Grey is a perfect
addition to the afternoon

641
00:31:45.290 --> 00:31:48.090
Aaah! Hold on!
What am I doing...?!

642
00:31:48.090 --> 00:31:50.190
I shouldn't be sitting here
all relaxed just casually

643
00:31:50.190 --> 00:31:52.690
sipping tea without a
single care in the world!

644
00:31:52.690 --> 00:31:55.200
Nami, Vivi, and the others
could be waiting out there

645
00:31:55.200 --> 00:31:58.330
right now for me
to come and help them!

646
00:31:58.330 --> 00:32:01.040
I am still curious about
one thing, though...

647
00:32:01.040 --> 00:32:03.040
What is a nice,
relaxing place like this

648
00:32:03.040 --> 00:32:06.040
doing smack in the middle
of an ancient, creepy jungle?

649
00:32:06.040 --> 00:32:09.040
[SNAIL ringing]

650
00:32:09.040 --> 00:32:11.210
Huh?

651
00:32:11.210 --> 00:32:16.300
[SNAIL ringing]

652
00:32:16.300 --> 00:32:17.430
[SANJI]
What?

653
00:32:25.100 --> 00:32:26.640
Hmm?

654
00:32:26.670 --> 00:32:28.380
A transponder snail.

655
00:32:32.210 --> 00:32:33.980
Yeah, hello...

656
00:32:33.980 --> 00:32:36.050
You've reached the crap café...

657
00:32:36.050 --> 00:32:37.480
Can I take your order...?

658
00:32:41.660 --> 00:32:47.590
You can quit fooling
around now, jackass.

659
00:32:47.590 --> 00:32:48.600
Now then...

660
00:32:48.600 --> 00:32:52.070
Your report's a little bit late,
don't you think?

661
00:32:52.070 --> 00:32:55.170
[SANJI]
Huh...? My report, you say?

662
00:32:55.170 --> 00:32:59.410
And to whom exactly
am I speaking, please?

663
00:32:59.410 --> 00:33:00.220
Me.

664
00:33:00.420 --> 00:33:02.790
Mr. 0.

665
00:33:03.790 --> 00:33:05.290
[SANJI]
Hmm...

666
00:33:11.070 --> 00:33:14.640
The scope of this planet's so vast and so grand

667
00:33:14.600 --> 00:33:17.990
That if treasure's out there, well where do you start?

668
00:33:17.940 --> 00:33:21.280
Keep your wits about you, don’t leave it to chance

669
00:33:21.300 --> 00:33:25.380
Yeah play it smart but don’t forget
that in the end you’re still rolling the dice

670
00:33:27.420 --> 00:33:28.550
And that's why...

671
00:33:31.290 --> 00:33:34.580
If someone gets in our way, well who cares?

672
00:33:34.630 --> 00:33:37.970
If someone’s running their mouth, well who cares?

673
00:33:37.950 --> 00:33:43.460
Let's sail out, yeah we'll tell all the losers here "bon voyage"

674
00:33:43.220 --> 00:33:45.150
Get lost and stay

675
00:33:44.910 --> 00:33:51.270
Cause even if you think what I'm doing
is dumb, I'm gonna get it done

676
00:33:51.280 --> 00:33:57.850
The more impossible the impressive, reach for the stars

677
00:33:57.960 --> 00:34:04.570
Yeah, even if you think what I'm doing
is dumb, I'm gonna take you on

678
00:34:04.600 --> 00:34:11.240
If we can sail across this vast sea we’ll find a paradise

679
00:34:11.590 --> 00:34:16.950
Go ahead and give it your best,
next time you look out your telescope

680
00:34:16.710 --> 00:34:18.750
You’ll find you’re one step closer
